From a77d56a00c352862413a68a81e8864e771d8839a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 00:08:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Curtain: mp4 clips, 2s dissolve, and a curtain that sits
 under the UI

The pause screen was a full-screen GIF on top of everything, which meant
the table lost the whole interface for the length of the break and the GM
paid GIF-sized bytes for every loop shipped in the bundle.

- V now opens the curtain panel, the same one the toolbar eye button
  opens. It still lowers a curtain that is already up, which is what the
  "Continuar (V)" button on the overlay has always promised.
- The clip catalog accepts mp4/webm alongside the old still formats, and
  the overlay renders video muted, looping and without controls. Videos
  are flagged in the panel so the GM can tell them apart at a glance.
- Raising and lowering fade over two seconds instead of snapping.
- The message moved to the top centre and the countdown to the bottom
  right, clear of the chat button.
- The overlay dropped from z-200 to z-5: above the board, below the dock,
  the windows, the toolbar and the chat. Only the map is hidden. The
  board tools (select, ping, ruler) go dead while the curtain is up;
  handouts and the GM tools stay live.
- gif_url became clip_url over the wire, since it no longer carries a
  GIF. The host still reads the old name through a serde alias and the
  store falls back to it, so an older host keeps working.
